      "writtenOn": "2024-03-08T00:02:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When we exit this loop, the mutex will be in state `MUTEX_R_LOCKED_WAITING`, right? \n\nBut at that point, there may not actually be any waiters (if this is the only task waiting). Is that what you are referring to on line 152?\n\n\u003e  It\u0027s possible that there will be no waiting tasks\n\t\t\t * (because waiting bit could be cleared by task that\n\t\t\t * got the mutex after unlocking it).",
